-- schema: project v1 v2
-- A data directory OpenCode used through all three generations: the
-- storage files 1.2 imported, the V1 tables, and the V2 tables 2.0
-- migrated them into, each migrated session's copy written as the
-- migration writes it (seq from 0, minted IDs for the rows it adds).
-- ses_up is in all three, its storage copy holding a message the
-- database lacks, and OpenCode 2 carried it on; ses_done was migrated
-- and not carried on; ses_syn ends with a user message the migration
-- split in two, then the notice, then OpenCode 2's own rows; ses_rev's
-- copy was cut by a revert OpenCode 2 committed before carrying on;
-- ses_late went on in the V1 tables after the migration; ses_vrev
-- stages an OpenCode 2 revert at a copied row; ses_new is OpenCode 2's
-- alone; ses_files is in the storage files alone. Written by hand; no
-- row of a real database.
